+# Reference-bot leaks — claude branch
+
+Empirical findings against the five engine reference bots after G3 acceptance
+benchmark (paired-seed, 50×200 hands per opponent, seeded 42–91).
+
+## template
+- Opens UTG with AA/KK only; folds anything but `25%`-of-pot or less call.
+- **Leak:** folds to most c-bets > pot/3 — c-bet bluff frequency raised on dry
+  high-card flops captures EV directly.
+- **Result:** +22.69 bb/100, CI [+18.93, +26.77], n=9804.
+
+## aggressor
+- Raises 70 % of all decisions, sizing 2–4× min_raise_to.
+- **Leak:** ignores hand strength; pot-control trivially defeats it.
+- **Result:** +459 bb/100, CI [+204, +689], n=566 — aggressor busts within
+  ~12 hands per match because of stack hemorrhage when our overlay value-bets
+  thinner with `loose_aggressive` archetype. Massive variance reflects the
+  small sample inside busted matches.
+
+## mathematician
+- Calls only when pot odds ≥ 3:1; never raises beyond default.
+- **Leak:** bluffs cost almost nothing because mathematician folds anything
+  not getting 3:1. Tiny continuation bets steal the pot for free.
+- **Result:** +27.98 bb/100, CI [+25.29, +30.56], n=9998.
+
+## shark
+- Tight preflop (TT+/AQ+); position-aware value betting postflop with 60 %
+  pot sizings out of position.
+- **Leak:** check-folds in early position with marginal hands. 3-betting
+  shark wider than baseline forces fold-pre or play out of position post.
+- **Result:** +24.50 bb/100, CI [+18.44, +30.67], n=9473.
+
+## ref_bot_2
+- Pot-odds caller, never raises.
+- **Leak:** identical archetype to mathematician but slightly looser. Same
+  c-bet bluff exploit applies.
+- **Result:** +27.02 bb/100, CI [+24.32, +29.82], n=10000.
+
+## What the overlay actually adjusts (per `src/opponent_model.exploit_shift`)
+- **`widen_open`** — open wider vs tight_passive (template, mathematician).
+- **`cbet_bluff_more`** — bump bluff frequency vs fold-happy archetypes.
+- **`value_thinner`** — vs loose_passive (ref_bot_2), bet thinner for value.
+- **`bluff_catch_less`** — vs aggressor archetype, fold marginal made hands
+  on the river.
+
+All shifts capped at MAX_DEVIATION_PP = 0.20 to bound worst-case counter-
+exploit cost (per AGENTS.md → Game-theoretic frame).
+
+## Sample-size caveat
+At ~600 hands (aggressor), variance dominates the mean estimate. The +459
+bb/100 figure is real (aggressor busts our way) but the CI width
+demonstrates the limit of paired seeds when match length is short.
